  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116050",
      "title": "Injecting Services Into Services",
      "lectureOrder": 186,
      "videoOrder": 178,
      "sourceHash": "330ed515049d308d84036d47b17803c59b4d81e614aafdd4f8a7af04d208fb55",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.64,
          "en": "Thus far in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "and also in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "we used services to inject them into Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 8.963,
          "en": "Now, I did mention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.963,
          "end": 11.07,
          "en": "that you can also inject them into Directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.07,
          "end": 12.78,
          "en": "and that will essentially work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 12.78,
          "end": 15.45,
          "en": "just as it does with Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 20.45,
          "en": "but you can also inject services into other services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.94,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "And to show you how that works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 24.24,
          "en": "I'll add a new service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.24,
          "end": 26.91,
          "en": "and I'll add that service with help of the CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.91,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "because that is also something you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 33.45,
          "en": "Let's say we wanna add a simple logging service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 35.28,
          "en": "for demo purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.28,
          "end": 40.16,
          "en": "Well, we could do that by running ng g service, or ng g s,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.67,
          "end": 44.85,
          "en": "then the name of the service like logging.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.85,
          "end": 47.55,
          "en": "And then in my case, skip-tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.55,
          "end": 50.553,
          "en": "to avoid the generation of this test file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 54.63,
          "en": "That will give us a new logging.service.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.63,
          "end": 56.07,
          "en": "And as you see in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.07,
          "end": 59.643,
          "en": "we got a class with @Injectable already added to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.59,
          "end": 64.53,
          "en": "Now, here, I actually don't need a constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.53,
          "end": 67.83,
          "en": "Instead, here I want to add a log method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 70.59,
          "en": "to this service class here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.59,
          "end": 73.593,
          "en": "which expects to get a message of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.43,
          "end": 77.58,
          "en": "And then there I wanna generate a timestamp",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.58,
          "end": 82.263,
          "en": "by running new Date and then toLocaleTimeString.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 87.12,
          "en": "And then console.log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.12,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "some dynamically generated string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 94.91,
          "en": "where I have my timestamp like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.33,
          "end": 99.03,
          "en": "And then the log message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.03,
          "end": 102.63,
          "en": "And, of course, this is just some dummy service here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.63,
          "end": 105.06,
          "en": "It wouldn't be too useful in a real app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.06,
          "end": 107.75999999999999,
          "en": "since it only logs to the developer console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.75999999999999,
          "end": 109.2,
          "en": "But in a real app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 112.41,
          "en": "you could try to send log messages to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 115.92,
          "en": "Something we'll cover later, how you can talk to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.92,
          "end": 117.18,
          "en": "You could do something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.18,
          "end": 119.37,
          "en": "Here, I'll just log to the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.37,
          "end": 121.83,
          "en": "so that we can see whether that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.83,
          "end": 124.89,
          "en": "And now I want to use that logging service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.89,
          "end": 126.93,
          "en": "in one of my other services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.93,
          "end": 129.573,
          "en": "in the tasks service, to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.8,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "And if you are providing the service like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 137.85,
          "en": "that's super straightforward to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.85,
          "end": 142.17000000000002,
          "en": "because it is provided to the root application injector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.17000000000002,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "And therefore I can easily use it here in another service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 147.72,
          "en": "In a task service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 150.9,
          "en": "I can inject the logging service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.9,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "with help of the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 154.65,
          "en": "or the inject function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 157.173,
          "en": "just as you would do it in a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.01,
          "end": 160.82999999999998,
          "en": "So here I'll inject the logging service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 162.36,
          "en": "by importing that class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.36,
          "end": 165.03300000000002,
          "en": "and using it as an injection token here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.05,
          "end": 167.91,
          "en": "And then we can use that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.91,
          "end": 169.89,
          "en": "For example, here in add task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.89,
          "end": 172.95,
          "en": "I can use the logging service and call log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.95,
          "end": 177.95,
          "en": "Added task with title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.02,
          "end": 182.58,
          "en": "And then I can output taskData.title here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.58,
          "end": 183.603,
          "en": "Maybe like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.25,
          "end": 187.77,
          "en": "And then also log here if we change the status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.77,
          "end": 192.77,
          "en": "and say change task status to new status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.44,
          "end": 200.273,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "With that done, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "if you open the developer tools in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 210.27,
          "en": "and you click Add Task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.27,
          "end": 211.893,
          "en": "you see the log message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 216.36,
          "en": "And if I change the status, you see that as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.36,
          "end": 217.44,
          "en": "So that works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.44,
          "end": 221.34300000000002,
          "en": "and that is how you can inject a service into a service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.36,
          "end": 225.03,
          "en": "Now, things would be problematic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.03,
          "end": 228.78300000000002,
          "en": "if you would not provide the logging service like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.86,
          "end": 233.37,
          "en": "If you would then provide it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.37,
          "end": 236.64,
          "en": "with that app configuration object in main.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.64,
          "end": 238.62,
          "en": "it would work again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.62,
          "end": 241.98,
          "en": "So if I provide the logging service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.98,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "through that provider's array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 246.63,
          "en": "when running bootstrapApplication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 246.63,
          "end": 248.67,
          "en": "when doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.67,
          "end": 252.12,
          "en": "everything would work, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.12,
          "end": 255.54,
          "en": "But if you would not be doing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.54,
          "end": 259.5,
          "en": "and you would instead try to use the element injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.5,
          "end": 262.32,
          "en": "by, for example, going to the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.32,
          "end": 264.24,
          "en": "and adding providers there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 264.24,
          "end": 267.6,
          "en": "and then providing the logging service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.6,
          "end": 270.57,
          "en": "if you would try to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 270.57,
          "end": 274.05,
          "en": "then you'd get a null injector error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.05,
          "end": 276.12,
          "en": "Because as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 276.12,
          "end": 278.28,
          "en": "Components and Directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.28,
          "end": 281.67,
          "en": "do reach out to this ElementInjector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.67,
          "end": 283.14,
          "en": "which is the injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 283.14,
          "end": 285.18,
          "en": "to which you register the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 285.18,
          "end": 287.67,
          "en": "when using this provider's array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 287.67,
          "end": 290.4,
          "en": "here in the component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 290.4,
          "end": 294.6,
          "en": "But services will not reach out to the ElementInjector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.6,
          "end": 296.37,
          "en": "because they aren't elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.37,
          "end": 298.05,
          "en": "they're not part of the dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.05,
          "end": 302.267,
          "en": "They only have access to the EnvironmentInjector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.267,
          "end": 304.32,
          "en": "or the ModuleInjector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.32,
          "end": 306.933,
          "en": "So, therefore, this approach won't work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.8,
          "end": 310.86,
          "en": "and you instead should use this approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 313.383,
          "en": "or provide it in the main.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.76,
          "end": 315.78,
          "en": "But if you do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 315.78,
          "end": 318.84,
          "en": "you can easily inject services into other services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 318.84,
          "end": 320.85,
          "en": "This is no problem at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 320.85,
          "end": 323.55,
          "en": "and, indeed, something that's regularly done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 323.55,
          "end": 324.903,
          "en": "in Angular apps.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
